/-!
# `Work.ThmF.Prove.step9X` — Peterfalvi II, Ch. V §3, step (9), the divisibility `p ∣ |G : H|`

This is the content `(X)` of the lead's pass-13 route (`ThmF/_design13/ThmF13Step9.lean`):
in the standing context `CtxF H Q t s r P`, with step (3)'s output `h3`, step (8)'s output `h8`,
`Q₁ = oddPart Q ≠ 1`, the order data `hG hH hD hV`, `P ⊓ W = 1`, the `V`-invariance `hWV` of `W`,
the fixed-point-freeness `hfpfW`, the commutator condition `hVW` and Lemma 2 b (`hL2b`), the prime
`p = |P|` divides the index `|G : H|`.

Assume not.  Then (N1) `p ∤ |Q|`, and (N2) `|G|_p = |V|_p`; a Sylow `p`-subgroup `S` of `V`
containing `P` is a Sylow subgroup of `G`.  With `T = S ⊓ W`:

* `T` is cyclic (N3a) and `S = T ⋊ P`;
* `A := Ω₁(S) = C_T(P) ⊔ P` is abelian (N3b / `step9Omega1`) and weakly closed in `S`;
* Hall–Wielandt in `G` reduces `HasNormalIndexP p G` to `HasNormalIndexP p N_G(A)`;
* `[S,S] ≤ C_T(P) =: Σ_p` (`step9Omega2`), `Σ_p ⊴ N_G(A)` (`hL2b` + `hVW`), so the image of
  `S` in `N_G(A)/Σ_p` is an abelian Sylow; Hall–Wielandt there, together with N4
  (`step9N4`, giving a normal subgroup of index `p` in `N_G(S)` containing `T ⊇ Σ_p`), yields
  `HasNormalIndexP p N_G(A)`;
* hence `G` has a normal subgroup of index `p`, contradicting `G` simple (and `|G|` even while
  `p` is odd).
-/

